        "original_id": "1edae3ed-7d41-5888-a152-0f17d1a30eb7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Felix Avenue, Marcos Highway, Ortigas Avenue Extension, Cainta, National Arts Center, Philippines\n- People: Francisco P. Felix, Imelda Marcos, Ferdinand Marcos\n- Roles: mayor of Cainta, President of the Philippines, First Lady\n- Topics: road naming, wealth, offshore bank accounts, inauguration\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Imelda Marcos inaugurated the National Arts Center.\n- Felix Avenue, also known as Imelda Avenue, is a four-lane major road connecting Marcos Highway to Ortigas Avenue Extension.\n- Felix Avenue was named after Francisco P. Felix, a former mayor of Cainta, and Imelda Marcos, the wife of former President Ferdinand Marcos and a former First Lady.\n- Imelda Marcos remains one of the richest politicians in the Philippines through collections of clothing, artwork, and jewelry, along with money in offshore bank accounts under the pseudonym \"Jane Ryan\".",
